  "Body": {
    "ContentType": "html",
    "Content": "<p><a href=\"https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/services/devops/pipelines/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Azure Pipelines</a>&nbsp;now&nbsp;supports Linux/ARM64, as was highly requested by the community. Other key features to enhance the overall user experience are now available:&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>General</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/release-notes/2020/sprint-171-update#restrict-new-user-invitations-from-project-and-team-administrators\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Restrict new user invitations from project and team administrators</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Azure Boards</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/release-notes/2020/sprint-171-update#state-transition-restriction-rules-private-preview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">State transition restriction rules (in private preview)</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Azure Pipelines</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/release-notes/2020/sprint-171-update#additional-agent-platform-arm64\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Additional agent platform: ARM64</a></li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/release-notes/2020/sprint-171-update#tag-filter-support-for-pipeline-resources\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tag filter support for pipeline resources</a></li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/release-notes/2020/sprint-171-update#control-which-tasks-are-allowed-in-pipelines\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Control which tasks are allowed in pipelines</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Learn more about <a href=\"https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/services/devops/pipelines/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Azure Pipelines</a>.</p>\r\n",
    "Markdown": "Azure Pipelines now supports Linux/ARM64, as was highly requested by the community. Other key features to enhance the overall user experience are now available:\n\nGeneral\n\nRestrict new user invitations from project and team administrators\n\nAzure Boards\n\nState transition restriction rules (in private preview)\n\nAzure Pipelines\n\nAdditional agent platform: ARM64\n\nTag filter support for pipeline resources\n\nControl which tasks are allowed in pipelines\n\nLearn more about Azure Pipelines ."
  },
